MINIMUM INSERTIONS TO MAKE A STRING PALINDROME

🔥 Extremely important

Asked in Amazon / Google / Microsoft

DP + Palindrome logic

Directly related to Longest Palindromic Subsequence

📌 Problem Statement

Given a string s, return the minimum number of insertions required to make the string a palindrome.

You may insert characters at any position.

✍ Example
Input: "leetcode"
Output: 5


Explanation:
One palindrome possible: "leetcodocteel"
Minimum insertions required = 5

🧠 Key Insight (INTERVIEW GOLD)

Minimum Insertions = Length of String − Length of Longest Palindromic Subsequence

Why?

LPS gives characters already in palindromic order

Remaining characters must be inserted

🧮 Formula
minInsertions = n - LPS(s)

📐 Algorithm

Compute LPS(s)
(using LCS of s and reverse(s))

Return:

n - LPS

💻 Java Code
public class MinInsertionsPalindrome {

    public static int minInsertions(String s) {

        int n = s.length();
        String rev = new StringBuilder(s).reverse().toString();

        int[][] dp = new int[n + 1][n + 1];

        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
            for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {

                if (s.charAt(i - 1) == rev.charAt(j - 1)) {
                    dp[i][j] = 1 + dp[i - 1][j - 1];
                } else {
                    dp[i][j] = Math.max(dp[i - 1][j], dp[i][j - 1]);
                }
            }
        }

        int lps = dp[n][n];
        return n - lps;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String s = "leetcode";
        System.out.println(minInsertions(s));
    }
}

